From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] iertutil: Uri.QueryParsed and WwwFormUrlDecoder, GetIids, canonical Uri

Windows.Foundation.Uri.QueryParsed returned E_NOTIMPL. It now returns a
WwwFormUrlDecoder: the activatable class (CreateWwwFormUrlDecoder) and the
read-only collection of IWwwFormUrlDecoderEntry (IVectorView and IIterable,
with an iterator) that the documentation describes. A leading '?' is not part
of the first name, '&' separates the pairs, the first '=' splits name from
value, percent-escapes (UTF-8) are decoded; GetFirstValueByName returns the
first value of that name and fails when there is none. DllGetActivationFactory
had a single factory for every class; WwwFormUrlDecoder now has its own.

The Uri also implements IUriRuntimeClassWithAbsoluteCanonicalUri. GetIids of the
Uri, the factories and the new objects lists the interfaces they implement (a
CoTaskMem array, without IUnknown and IInspectable, as documented), and the
factories answer GetRuntimeClassName and GetTrustLevel; ActivateInstance of a
factory rejects a NULL out pointer. The QueryInterface "not implemented" and
DllGetClassObject messages, which describe correct E_NOINTERFACE /
CLASS_E_CLASSNOTAVAILABLE answers, are no longer FIXMEs.
